# A grant records a digest of raw file bytes (`hash.rs`), and the promise is
# that two clones of one commit agree on it. Git's default `core.autocrlf` on
# Windows rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, which changes every byte count and
# every digest in `.warlock/pacts.toml` — the whole tree would read stale on a
# Windows clone, permanently, and each pass would re-grant a hash that is then
# stale for everyone else.
#
# So line endings are normalised to LF on commit and never converted on
# checkout, on every platform. `text=auto` leaves files git detects as binary
# alone; the two below say so outright rather than relying on that detection.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.bin binary
